    "faq.eyebrow": "Frequently asked",
    "faq.title": "Before you write to us",
    "faq.q1": "Is everything really free?",
    "faq.a1": "Yes. Bible studies, the books, the visits and the prayers cost you nothing, ever. We will never ask you for money — not at the first study and not at the last one.",
    "faq.q2": "Do I have to become an Adventist?",
    "faq.a2": "No. Many people study with us for years and stay in their own church, or in none. Our goal is that you meet Jesus. What you do after that is between you and Him.",
    "faq.q3": "I live far from Delray Beach. Can you still help?",
    "faq.a3": "Yes — we serve the whole state, from Pensacola to Key West. If no missionary is near your town, we will study with you by video call and put you in touch with the nearest congregation.",
    "faq.q4": "What if I do not speak English well?",
    "faq.a4": "Write to us in your own language. We work in English, Spanish, Haitian Creole, French, Portuguese, German, Dutch, Russian and Ukrainian, and we will find someone who speaks yours.",
    "faq.q5": "I have doubts and hard questions. Is that a problem?",
    "faq.a5": "Not at all — bring them. Faith that has never been questioned is not very strong. We would rather talk honestly about a hard question than pretend it does not exist.",
    "faq.q6": "Are you the official Adventist Church?",
    "faq.a6": "We are an independent group of lay members who support the work of the Seventh-day Adventist Church. We are not a conference office and we do not speak for the denomination — we simply share the same faith and point people to a local church.",

